# Rule: SwiftUI Persistent Storage

Sources

https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/persistent-storage

Core Principle

SwiftUI persistent storage is for lightweight persisted state.

Rules

- Use `AppStorage` for app-level preferences and small settings-like values.
- Use `SceneStorage` for per-scene restoration of lightweight UI state.
- Persist the minimum information needed to restore useful UI continuity.
- Keep persisted UI state separate from persistent model/domain data.
- Store stable identifiers or compact preference values, not full models.
- Use unique keys for distinct persisted values.

Must Not

- Do not use `AppStorage`/`SceneStorage` as model persistence.
- Do not store large payloads or domain record blobs in user defaults wrappers.
- Do not duplicate model truth in storage keys when an identifier is enough.
